 hansGS:{n:"Hans Gerhard Hansen Smilden",st:"doc",line:"hatlem",par:["hansJen","halfri"],role:"2nd great-granduncle (great-grandmother Ingeborg's brother) · emigrant to North Dakota",b:"16 Nov 1873, Smilden, Hyllestad",d:"7 Dec 1928, North Dakota",ev:[["1873","Born 16 November and baptised 23 November",["b1873hg"]],["1875","At home at Smilden",["c1875s"]],["1891","Living at home at Smilden with his parents Hans Jensen and Halfri and his sister Ingeborg",["c1891sm"]],["1893","Emigrated from Bergen on 24 May on the Allan Line, aged 19, with two other Hyllestad men",["em1893hg"]],["1896","According to the county history he first worked in Minnesota lumber camps, then came to Larimore in 1896 and homesteaded in Section 2 of Moraine township, Grand Forks County, North Dakota",["nhs"]],["1897","Married Maren Totland (b. Feb 1879 in Norway; arrived 1895)",["nhs"]],["1900","US census: Hans H. Smilden, farmer, Moraine township, Grand Forks Co., N.D., immigrated 1893, with his wife Maren and their children Gustie and Hans",["nhs"]],["1904","US land patent of 1 August for his homestead (Township 151 N, Range 56 W, Section 2)",["nhs"]],["1910","US census: Hans H. 'Smelden', Larimore, naturalised citizen, with Maren and seven children",["nhs"]],["1920","US census: farmer in Hegton township, Grand Forks Co., with Maren and eight children at home",["nhs"]],["1928","Died 7 December",["nhs"]]],note:"Identified as the Norwegian Hans Gerhard by his birth (Nov 1873), his 1893 emigration and his use of the Smilden name; the Smilden descendants in America reached the same conclusion. His wife Maren died in 1946 or 1948 (sources differ). Their children, all born in North Dakota, were Gustie, Hans, Hannah, Thomas, Inga, Tina, Henry, Ingvold, Joseph and Marie. Only those confirmed as deceased are shown here. The US details come from a published forum transcription of the census, not from images I have seen."},
